markdown-mode NEWS -- history of user-visible changes.

This is the news of e8-markdown-mode, the E8 port of markdown-mode.
'C-h P' shows it under the package's description.


* Changes in markdown-mode 0.1.0

This is the first release, a port of markdown-mode 2.9-alpha.  It
needs E8 0.5.20 or newer.

** 'markdown-mode' edits Markdown, and 'gfm-mode' GitHub Flavored Markdown.
Files ending in '.md', '.markdown', '.mkd', '.mdown', '.mkdn', '.mdwn'
and '.mdx' open in 'markdown-mode'.

** Markdown is styled as it is shown.
Headings, emphasis, inline code, code blocks, links, footnotes, lists
and checkboxes, block quotes, tables, HTML, comments and YAML front
matter have markdown-mode's faces, for a theme to style.  Emphasis
and links may run over a paragraph's lines, and nothing inside code is
styled as Markdown.

** 'TAB' on a heading folds it, and 'S-TAB' folds the buffer.
Elsewhere 'TAB' indents, to the next likely column each time.

** Headings and list items are moved, promoted and demoted.
'C-c C-n', 'C-c C-p', 'C-c C-f', 'C-c C-b' and 'C-c C-u' go between
headings; 'C-c C--' and 'C-c C-=' promote and demote; 'C-c <up>' and
'C-c <down>' move a heading's subtree or a list item.

** 'M-RET' inserts a list item.
The next number, the same bullet, or an unticked checkbox after one.

** 'C-c C-s' inserts markup.
Bold, italic, inline code, strike-through and '<kbd>' around the
region or the word at point, headings, fenced code blocks, block
quotes, rules, checkboxes and footnotes.

** Links are inserted and followed.
'C-c C-l' and 'C-c C-i' insert an inline link or image; 'C-c C-o'
follows the link at point, to a URL or a file; 'M-n' and 'M-p' go
between links.

** 'C-c C-d' does what makes sense at point.
It ticks a checkbox, follows a link, or goes between a footnote's
marker and its definition.

** Markup and URLs can be hidden.
'C-c C-x C-m' hides markup, link URLs included; 'C-c C-x C-l' shows
inline links' URLs as a single character.

** Code blocks can be styled in their language's own faces.
'C-c C-x C-f' toggles 'markdown-fontify-code-blocks-natively'.

** 'M-x imenu' lists the headings.

** There is no export, preview or table editing.
The README lists what markdown-mode.el has that the port does not.
